window.AG_PRACTICE["jingluo"] = {"id":"jingluo","axis":"needle","seal":"針","scene":"art/scene-needles.jpg","title":"Channel Flow","titleZh":"經絡流注","sub":"The twelve channels in order, and the four directions they run","subZh":"十二經流注之序，與四類走向","mentor":{"key":"zhen","nm":"Zhēn Yǐn","nmZh":"針隱","line":"\"Qi does not wander. It runs a circuit, and the circuit closes. If you can say the twelve in order without stopping, you already understand more than you think.\"","lineZh":"「氣不亂走。它走一個圈，而且會回到起點。十二經能一口氣背下來，你懂的就比你以為的多。」"},"card":{"h":"One Circuit, Twelve Stages 一周十二","hZh":"","p":"The cycle starts in the Lung at the hour of the Tiger 寅時 and closes twelve organs later in the Liver, which hands back to the Lung. Hand yin runs chest to hand; hand yang, hand to head; foot yang, head to foot; foot yin, foot to chest. Four rules cover all twelve.","pZh":"寅時起於肺，歷十二臟腑而終於肝，肝復注於肺。手三陰從胸走手，手三陽從手走頭，足三陽從頭走足，足三陰從足走腹（胸）。四則盡之。"},"items":[{"k":"order","q":"Put the first six channels of the daily cycle in order, starting from the Lung.","qZh":"由肺起，排出流注前六經。","seq":[{"t":"Lung","c":"肺"},{"t":"Large Intestine","c":"大腸"},{"t":"Stomach","c":"胃"},{"t":"Spleen","c":"脾"},{"t":"Heart","c":"心"},{"t":"Small Intestine","c":"小腸"}],"note":"Notice the shape: a yin organ hands to its yang partner, which hands to the next yin-yang pair. Lung→Large Intestine, Stomach→Spleen, Heart→Small Intestine. The pairs are the same interior-exterior pairs you already know. 觀其式：陰經交其表裡之陽經，陽經復交次一對。肺→大腸、胃→脾、心→小腸。其配即表裡之配。"},{"k":"order","q":"Now the second six, from the Bladder back to the Liver.","qZh":"再排後六經，自膀胱至肝。","seq":[{"t":"Bladder","c":"膀胱"},{"t":"Kidney","c":"腎"},{"t":"Pericardium","c":"心包"},{"t":"San Jiao","c":"三焦"},{"t":"Gallbladder","c":"膽"},{"t":"Liver","c":"肝"}],"note":"And the Liver hands back to the Lung, closing the circuit. Twelve channels, twenty-four hours, two hours each. 肝復注於肺，其環乃合。十二經、二十四時，一經二時辰。"},{"k":"mc","q":"At which hours is the Lung channel at its peak?","qZh":"肺經旺於何時？","opts":[{"t":"3–5 a.m., the hour of the Tiger 寅時","c":"寅時，凌晨三至五時","ok":1,"note":"The cycle begins here. Clinically it is one reason a dry cough or asthma that reliably wakes a patient in the small hours draws attention to the Lung. Treat the observation as a prompt to look, not as a diagnosis on its own. 流注始於此。故乾咳、喘證每於此時而作者，當一察其肺。此為提示而非診斷。"},{"t":"11 a.m.–1 p.m., the hour of the Horse 午時","c":"午時，上午十一至下午一時","ok":0,"note":"That is the Heart. 午時屬心。"},{"t":"11 p.m.–1 a.m., the hour of the Rat 子時","c":"子時，夜半十一至一時","ok":0,"note":"That is the Gallbladder — and the classical reason for the advice to be asleep before midnight. 子時屬膽，古人勸子時前就寢，義本於此。"},{"t":"1–3 a.m., the hour of the Ox 丑時","c":"丑時，凌晨一至三時","ok":0,"note":"That is the Liver, which stores blood during rest. 丑時屬肝，臥則血歸於肝。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each channel group to the direction it runs.","qZh":"四類經脈配其走向。","pairs":[{"l":"Three hand yin 手三陰","lZh":"","r":"Chest → hand","rZh":"從胸走手"},{"l":"Three hand yang 手三陽","lZh":"","r":"Hand → head","rZh":"從手走頭"},{"l":"Three foot yang 足三陽","lZh":"","r":"Head → foot","rZh":"從頭走足"},{"l":"Three foot yin 足三陰","lZh":"","r":"Foot → abdomen and chest","rZh":"從足走腹（胸）"}],"note":"These four rules explain the hand-offs: hand yin meets hand yang at the fingertips, hand yang meets foot yang at the head, foot yang meets foot yin at the toes, foot yin meets hand yin in the chest. Four meeting places, one closed loop. 四則即其交接之處：手陰與手陽交於指端，手陽與足陽交於頭面，足陽與足陰交於足趾，足陰與手陰交於胸中。四交而成一環。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which three channels are the three hand yin?","qZh":"手三陰為何？","opts":[{"t":"Lung, Pericardium, Heart","c":"肺、心包、心","ok":1,"note":"All three run from the chest along the inner arm to the hand: Lung on the radial (thumb) side, Pericardium in the middle, Heart on the ulnar (little finger) side. That layout is why LU9 is at the thumb side of the wrist crease and HT7 at the little-finger side. 三者皆自胸循臂內側而至手：肺在橈側（拇指側），心包居中，心在尺側（小指側）。故太淵在腕橫紋橈側，神門在尺側。"},{"t":"Large Intestine, San Jiao, Small Intestine","c":"大腸、三焦、小腸","ok":0,"note":"Those are the three hand yang, running from the hand to the head along the outer arm. 此手三陽，自手循臂外側而上頭。"},{"t":"Spleen, Liver, Kidney","c":"脾、肝、腎","ok":0,"note":"Those are the three foot yin, and they cross at SP6 三陰交. 此足三陰，交會於三陰交。"},{"t":"Stomach, Gallbladder, Bladder","c":"胃、膽、膀胱","ok":0,"note":"Those are the three foot yang: Stomach in front, Gallbladder at the side, Bladder behind. 此足三陽：胃行身前，膽行身側，膀胱行身後。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Where do the three foot yin channels cross, and why does that matter?","qZh":"足三陰交會於何穴？其義安在？","opts":[{"t":"Sanyinjiao SP6 — one needle reaches Spleen, Liver and Kidney","c":"三陰交 — 一針而及脾肝腎","ok":1,"note":"Three cun above the tip of the medial malleolus, behind the medial border of the tibia. Because three channels meet there, it appears in almost every prescription for blood deficiency, yin deficiency and gynaecological patterns. Standard caution: SP6 is traditionally avoided in pregnancy. 在內踝尖上三寸，脛骨內側緣後方。三經交會，故養血、滋陰、婦科諸方多用之。常規禁忌：孕婦傳統上忌用三陰交。"},{"t":"Yinlingquan SP9","c":"陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"SP9 is the Sea point of the Spleen and the main point for draining damp — a single-channel point. 陰陵泉為脾之合穴，主利濕，屬一經之穴。"},{"t":"Taixi KI3","c":"太谿","ok":0,"note":"KI3 is the Kidney's Source point, on the Kidney channel alone. 太谿為腎之原穴，獨在腎經。"},{"t":"Zusanli ST36","c":"足三里","ok":0,"note":"ST36 is on the Stomach channel — a foot yang channel. 足三里在胃經，屬足三陽。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Where does the Liver channel hand over, closing the twelve-channel cycle?","qZh":"肝經交於何經，以合十二經之環？","opts":[{"t":"To the Lung, in the chest","c":"上注於肺，交於胸中","ok":1,"note":"The Liver channel runs up through the diaphragm, distributes in the ribs and chest, and connects to the Lung — which restarts the cycle at 3 a.m. This anatomical link is also the reasoning behind Liver patterns producing rib-side and chest complaints. 肝經上貫膈，布脅肋，注於肺中，寅時復始。此經行亦即肝證多見脅肋胸中之症之所本。"},{"t":"To the Kidney, at the foot","c":"下交於腎，在足","ok":0,"note":"Kidney hands to Pericardium, earlier in the cycle. 腎交心包，在環之前段。"},{"t":"To the Gallbladder, at the eye","c":"交於膽，在目","ok":0,"note":"Gallbladder hands *to* the Liver, at the big toe. The direction is the other way. 膽交於肝，在足大趾。其向相反。"},{"t":"To the Du mai, at the crown","c":"交於督脈，在巔頂","ok":0,"note":"The Liver channel does reach the vertex, but the twelve-channel hand-off is to the Lung. 肝經雖上巔，然十二經之交在肺。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"What is the practical use of knowing channel pathways rather than just point locations?","qZh":"知經脈循行，較僅知穴位，其用安在？","opts":[{"t":"It lets you choose distal points for a complaint far from the needle","c":"可據以遠道取穴","ok":1,"note":"If the pathway passes through the complaint, a point on that channel can treat it from a distance — LI4 in the hand for toothache and facial pain, LU7 at the wrist for the head and nape, GB34 at the knee for rib-side pain. The pathway is the reason the point works. 經行所過，主治所及。故合谷在手而治齒痛面痛，列缺在腕而治頭項，陽陵泉在膝而治脅痛。經行即其效之所由。"},{"t":"It tells you the depth to needle","c":"可知進針之深淺","ok":0,"note":"Depth follows the local anatomy and the patient's build, and is learned point by point with supervision. 深淺從局部解剖與形體，須逐穴而習，且宜有師監之。"},{"t":"It replaces pattern differentiation","c":"可代辨證","ok":0,"note":"Channel selection follows the pattern; it does not replace working the pattern out. 選經從證而定，不能代辨證之工。"},{"t":"It fixes the order of needle insertion","c":"可定進針之次第","ok":0,"note":"Insertion order follows clinical priorities and patient position. 進針之序從緩急與體位。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each channel to the hour it peaks.","qZh":"經脈配旺時。","pairs":[{"l":"Lung 肺","lZh":"","r":"3–5 a.m. 寅","rZh":""},{"l":"Stomach 胃","lZh":"","r":"7–9 a.m. 辰","rZh":""},{"l":"Heart 心","lZh":"","r":"11 a.m.–1 p.m. 午","rZh":""},{"l":"Kidney 腎","lZh":"","r":"5–7 p.m. 酉","rZh":""},{"l":"Liver 肝","lZh":"","r":"1–3 a.m. 丑","rZh":""}],"note":"Use these as prompts, not verdicts. A symptom that reliably arrives at the same hour every day is worth noticing — the dawn diarrhoea in chapter ten is exactly such a finding — but the hour alone never makes the diagnosis. 此為提示而非判詞。症候每日定時而作者，最可留意——第十章之五更瀉即其例——然徒憑時辰不足以定證。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which statement about the eight extraordinary vessels is correct?","qZh":"奇經八脈，何說為是？","opts":[{"t":"They regulate and store the qi and blood of the twelve channels","c":"蓄溢調節十二經之氣血","ok":1,"note":"The classical image is reservoirs beside a river: when the twelve channels overflow, the extraordinary vessels take the surplus; when the channels run short, the vessels release. Only the Du and Ren have their own points; the other six are reached through the Eight Confluent points. 其譬如江河之湖澤：十二經滿則溢入奇經，經虛則奇經灌之。惟督任有專穴，其餘六脈皆由八脈交會穴取之。"},{"t":"They each pair with a zang or fu organ","c":"各配一臟一腑","ok":0,"note":"They do not have the direct organ pairing that the twelve regular channels have — that is part of what makes them extraordinary. 奇經不與臟腑直接絡屬，此其所以為奇。"},{"t":"They all run down the midline","c":"皆行於身之中線","ok":0,"note":"Du and Ren run the midline; Dai mai encircles the waist; the Qiao and Wei vessels run the sides. 督任行中線，帶脈環腰，蹻維行於身側。"},{"t":"They cannot be treated with needles","c":"不可以針治","ok":0,"note":"They are treated constantly, through Du and Ren points and through the Eight Confluent points. 常以督任本穴及八脈交會穴治之。"}]}]};
